If you don't install the ranged pet attack patch (I forgot the correct 
name of that one), pets will never use ranged weapons, and no breath 
attacks neither. So, dragons (especially saddled silver dragons) are 
pretty safe and good pets. Silver dragons are good, since they resist 
cold and all the rays that would hit them are reflected, leaving only 
green slime, cockatrices and ToD (and generally physical damage) as 
threats to them, which can be avoided if you're careful. If not, you'll 
be standing next to a tame green slime all at once, which is threatening 
to turn all of Juiblex' Lair into green slime, so you polymorph it into 
a Gnome King, genocide the evil green slimes and are on your way.

